.TH TMUX-FOLLOW-CLICK 1 "2026-06-30" "termnav" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tmux-follow-click \- resolve tmux mouse clicks to URL or file actions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tmux-follow-click
.RI [ tmux-format-args ...]
.br
.B tmux-follow-click
.B --stdin
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tmux-follow-click
is intended for tmux mouse bindings. It receives tmux mouse formats and pane
context, identifies the clicked token or line region, and opens URLs in the
terminal or file targets through
.BR nvim-tmux-open (1).
.PP
With
.B --stdin ,
the helper reads the tmux mouse fields from standard input, one field per line:
hyperlink, word, line, x, cwd, client tty, pane id, y, pane top, and pane left.
This mode is preferred for robust tmux bindings because quoted here-doc input
preserves indentation and literal shell text.
.PP
The built-in token policy recognizes common terminal shapes such as HTTP URLs,
localhost endpoints, git SSH remotes, CVE identifiers, RFC references, file
paths, and terminal-specific Neovim link schemes.
.SH EXTENSIONS
.B tmux-follow-click
loads optional shell extensions from
an absolute
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/termnav/tmux-follow/extensions.d/*.sh ,
falling back to
.IR $HOME/.config/termnav/tmux-follow/extensions.d/*.sh .
Empty and relative XDG config paths are ignored. When neither base directory is
available, no optional extensions are loaded.
Set
.B TERMNAV_TMUX_FOLLOW_EXTENSION_DIR
to use another directory.
.PP
Extension files can call
.B tmux_follow_register_token_detector
with a detector function. Detectors claim a token by setting
.B target
and
.B target_kind
and returning success.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TERMNAV_TMUX_FOLLOW_EXTENSION_DIR
Override directory for token detector extensions.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Absolute base directory for token detector extensions.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The click was handled or intentionally ignored, including clicks that do not
resolve to a URL or file target.
.TP
.B 1
Unexpected helper failure before the click can be handled. Target opener
failures are normally translated into best-effort terminal or tmux messages.
.TP
.B 2
Usage or environment error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nvim-tmux-open (1),
.BR nvim-ssh-control-open (1)
